{"seq":2,"slug":"franklin-roosevelt-rise","title":"富兰克林·罗斯福：崛起之路","stage":"DONE","category":"franklin-roosevelt","categoryLabel":"富兰克林·罗斯福","chapterCount":3,"docCount":8,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise","rating":{"composite":3.56,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/11_franklin-roosevelt/2_franklin-roosevelt-rise","introMarkdown":"# 富兰克林·罗斯福：崛起之路\n\n1882 年 1 月 30 日，富兰克林·德拉诺·罗斯福（Franklin Delano Roosevelt，常缩写为 FDR）出生于纽约州哈德逊河畔的海德公园（Hyde Park）。他是一个殷实的荷兰裔旧家族的独子，自幼在家庭教师、欧洲旅行与乡绅庄园的环境中长大。从这样一个看似与权力中心相距甚远的起点，到 1932 年成为民主党总统候选人并赢得压倒性胜利，其间经历了整整半个世纪的塑造、试探与磨难。\n\n这一卷专注于罗斯福\"崛起\"的阶段——也就是他入主白宫之前的人生。它不讨论新政、二战或外交遗产，而是回答一个更基础的问题：一个含着金汤匙出生的乡绅子弟，是如何一步步成长为足以驾驭大萧条与世界大战的政治家的？\n\n崛起之路大致可分为三段。第一段是出身与教育：海德公园的庄园童年、格罗顿公学（Groton）校长恩迪科特·皮博迪灌输的\"公共服务\"伦理、哈佛三年与哥伦比亚法学院的求学，以及与远房堂妹埃莉诺的结合。这段经历奠定了他的世界观、人脉与表达能力。\n\n第二段是政治学徒期。1910 年，他以民主党人身份当选纽约州参议员，旋即因反抗坦慕尼协会而崭露头角；1913 至 1920 年，他在威尔逊政府中担任海军部副部长，积累了行政与战时动员的实战经验；1920 年，他作为副总统候选人与考克斯搭档竞选，虽败犹荣，全国知名度大增。\n\n第三段是危机与重生。1921 年夏，三十九岁的罗斯福突患脊髓灰质炎（小儿麻痹症），下肢永久瘫痪。在多数人看来，这意味着政治生涯的终结。然而他在佐治亚州温泉镇（Warm Springs）的康复尝试、1924 与 1928 年两度为史密斯做提名演说的\"快乐的斗士\"，以及 1928、1930 年两度当选纽约州长的政绩，最终使他在 1932 年芝加哥代表大会上脱颖而出。\n\n本卷力求以确凿的日期、地点、文献与人物为依据，呈现一段被后世传奇化、却充满偶然与艰辛的真实历程。读完这三章，读者应能理解：罗斯福的崛起既非纯粹的命运眷顾，也非简单的天才注定，而是出身资源、制度机遇、个人意志与历史时机层层叠加的产物。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"aristocratic-origins-and-education","title":"贵族出身与求学岁月","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/aristocratic-origins-and-education","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"hyde-park-and-groton","title":"海德公园的庄园童年与格罗顿岁月","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/aristocratic-origins-and-education/hyde-park-and-groton"},{"seq":2,"slug":"harvard-columbia-and-eleanor","title":"哈佛、哥伦比亚法学院与埃莉诺","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/aristocratic-origins-and-education/harvard-columbia-and-eleanor"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"apprenticeship-in-politics","title":"政治学徒期","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/apprenticeship-in-politics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"state-senate-debut","title":"1910 年州参议员：选举政治的初体验","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/apprenticeship-in-politics/state-senate-debut"},{"seq":2,"slug":"assistant-secretary-of-the-navy","title":"海军部副部长：七年的行政历练","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/apprenticeship-in-politics/assistant-secretary-of-the-navy"},{"seq":3,"slug":"vice-presidential-campaign","title":"1920 年副总统竞选：一场虽败犹荣的全国亮相","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/apprenticeship-in-politics/vice-presidential-campaign"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"from-paralysis-to-nomination","title":"从瘫痪到提名","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/from-paralysis-to-nomination","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"polio-and-warm-springs","title":"小儿麻痹与温泉镇：在灾难中重塑自我","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/from-paralysis-to-nomination/polio-and-warm-springs"},{"seq":2,"slug":"governor-of-new-york","title":"纽约州长：通往白宫的最后跳板","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/from-paralysis-to-nomination/governor-of-new-york"},{"seq":3,"slug":"nomination-and-new-deal-prelude","title":"1932 年提名与\"新政\"序曲：崛起的终点与起点","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-rise/from-paralysis-to-nomination/nomination-and-new-deal-prelude"}]}]}